{
  "info": {
    "name": "SCRUM-204 Onboarding role grants",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Onboarding page and Keycloak role grants (docs/onboarding-role-grants.md). The account type is the professional realm role (investor, realtor or lender), one per account; the persona is gone.\n\nVariables: base_url; access_token = an ordinary account WITHOUT a professional role and without a realtor license; admin_token = an account with the realm role admin. Run the folders in order with the Collection Runner.\n\nBy default the lender request waits (PENDING) and the admin approves it in folder 4 (503 with keycloak.role-admin.enabled=false, and the request stays PENDING). With lender listed in ONBOARDING_SELF_SERVICE_ROLES it is APPROVED at once. Checks read lender_status, saved by 'Request lender', and expect the matching answer.\n\nFolder 6 revokes the lender role again (200, or 503 with role management off), so the collection can be re-run with the same account after refreshing access_token.\n\nData created: role requests and grant history of the ordinary account, kept as history."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "admin_token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "request_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "lender_status",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "approve_code",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "onboarded_at",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Onboarding state",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Entitlements have the onboarding fields, no persona",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/users/me/entitlements"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const r = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('onboarding fields', () => { pm.expect(r.onboardingCompleted).to.be.a('boolean'); pm.expect(r.pendingRoles).to.be.an('array'); pm.expect(r.roles).to.include('user'); });",
                  "pm.test('no persona fields', () => { pm.expect(r).to.not.have.property('persona'); pm.expect(r).to.not.have.property('personaLocked'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH /api/users/me ignores a persona",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/users/me",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"persona\": \"REALTOR\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const r = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('no persona in the profile', () => pm.expect(r).to.not.have.property('persona'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', r.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "A persona grants nothing",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/users/me/entitlements"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const r = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('no realtor or lender feature', () => { pm.expect(r.features.realtorCrm).to.eql(false); pm.expect(r.features.lender).to.eql(false); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
